Newton's laws again: For every action there is an equal and opposite reaction.

* while these describe the physics of natural motion, this one in particular is well applied to the idea of cause/effect + interactivity.

---

What does cause and effect really even mean?

---

Interactive Graphic Design is GD that involves users/viewers in ways that traditional GD doesn't.

This starts getting difficult to describe because to a certain extent all GD is interactive... people must look at something, they must turn pages, etc. This is just passover interactivity. So is, at its basic level, clicking around on a website.

tennis and conversing with another person are both examples of interactivity, but they aren't the things we are referring to when we talk about interaction design, etc. What we mean then is that an interface of somekind is involved. The interaction is between the person and the interface.

